select null, t.id, 'builtin', 'Which test detects factor XIII deficiency, which leaves the PT and aPTT normal?', '["Thrombin time","Reptilase time","Bleeding time","5 M urea clot solubility test"]'::jsonb, 3, 'FXIII deficiency gives a normal PT and aPTT. The 5 M urea clot solubility test is a classic screen, but it only detects severe deficiency, so quantitative FXIII activity is now the recommended first test. Reference: Factor XIII Deficiency: A Review of Biology, Testing, and Treatment (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12825037).', '["Tests fibrinogen to fibrin conversion.","Like thrombin time, but not affected by heparin.","Tests platelet function.","Clots without cross-linking dissolve in 5 M urea."]'::jsonb, 3, 'verified'
